<%# Fuime: the consent text a guardian is shown before submitting identity details.

    Strict locals with none declared, per dev-docs/code_style.md: this partial is pure
    copy and must stay that way. Interpolating a venture name or a guardian's details
    would change the hash per render, and the hash is the thing the consent record points
    at (see below).

    THIS FILE'S CONTENTS ARE HASHED. Fuime::RequirementCollectionsController digests it
    and stores the first 16 hex characters on the GuardianVerification as
    `doc_version_hash`, which is how the consent record proves WHAT was agreed to
    without keeping a per-guardian copy (L4). Editing the wording changes the hash, so
    old records keep pointing at the version actually shown. That is deliberate: do not
    "fix" it by hashing something more stable.

    Copy constraints that apply here:
      * L5 forbids bank / banking / deposits / insured / FDIC while no partner bank
        exists. Say "financial platform". The guardian is the legal payee, not the
        owner of a Stripe connected account.
      * The card program, if mentioned, must carry
        Fuime::CardSpendPolicy::REQUIRED_DISCLOSURE verbatim and must avoid every entry
        in FORBIDDEN_PHRASES. A spec checks this file against both. %>

<div class="card border b--info p-4 mb3">
  <h3 class="mt0">What happens to the details you enter</h3>

  <ul class="mb2">
    <li>
      <strong>They go to Stripe, not to us.</strong> Stripe is the payments company that
      processes purchases. Fuime passes your details straight to them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>We don't keep your Social Security number or your ID.</strong> Your ID photo
      is uploaded directly to Stripe. Fuime keeps only a record that you completed this
      step, the date, and a reference number — never the image, and never your SSN.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>You are the legal payee.</strong> Ninth Street Labs, LLC, doing business as
      Fuime, is the seller of record. You are the legal payee and clawback obligor, and
      you must approve the payout destination before the first payout. Your child runs
      the venture day to day.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Why you and not your child.</strong> The legal payee must be an adult, and
      the identity details below are yours. Your child cannot complete this step and
      should not be asked for any of it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="text-sm secondary mb-0">
    Fuime is a financial technology company, not a bank. Fuime does not hold deposits and
    does not offer FDIC-insured products. Payments are processed by Stripe. Ninth Street
    Labs, LLC, doing business as Fuime, is the seller of record on purchases. Guardians
    are the legal payee on operator payouts and must approve the destination before the
    first payout; young founders run the venture day to day.
  </p>
</div>

<p class="text-sm secondary">
  A business card issued on this account
  <%= Fuime::CardSpendPolicy::REQUIRED_DISCLOSURE %>.
</p>
